@node MAIN "Micropolis - Help"

  @{b}Micropolis for AmigaOS@{ub}

  Build and run a city. The simulation is the original Micropolis
  (SimCity) code; the user interface is a native Intuition/RTG one.

  @{" Getting started     " link START}
  @{" Building tools      " link TOOLS}
  @{" Keyboard and mouse  " link KEYS}
  @{" Windows             " link WINDOWS}
  @{" Menus               " link MENUS}
  @{" Traffic rules       " link TRAFFIC}
  @{" Animation           " link ANIMATION}
  @{" The R C I bars      " link DEMAND}
  @{" Scenarios           " link SCENARIOS}
  @{" Screen mode and settings " link SETTINGS}
  @{" Cheat words         " link CHEATS}
  @{" Index               " link INDEX}
@endnode

@node START "Getting started"
@toc MAIN

  1. Pick a tool on the left (the Query tool is active at the start).
  2. Click or drag on the map. The white frame shows what will be built.
  3. Zones (Resid, Comm, Indus) only grow when they have power
     (power plant plus wires) and roads. Keep an eye on the R C I bars.
  4. Open the budget (menu Windows/Budget) to set taxes and funding.

  Speed: keys 0 (pause) to 3 (fast), or the Speed menu.
@endnode

@node TOOLS "Building tools"
@toc MAIN

  Query   zone status box (density, land value, crime, pollution)
  Doze    bulldozer: removes anything, cost 1
  Road    10 per tile        Rail  20 per tile       Wire  5 per tile
  Park    10                 Resid/Comm/Indus  100 each (3x3 zones)
  Fire    500 fire station   Polic 500 police station
  Stadm   5000 stadium       Coal  3000 coal power plant
  Nucl    5000 nuclear plant Sea   3000 sea port   Airp  10000 airport
  Hwy     40 highway (last icon, see Traffic rules)

  Chalk   draw a note on the map (white line); notes are not saved with the city
  Eraser  removes the chalk lines you touch

  Roads and wires over water are built as bridges and cost more.
  Auto Bulldoze (menu Options) clears rubble automatically.
@endnode

@node KEYS "Keyboard and mouse"
@toc MAIN

  Left mouse button   use the tool / click buttons
  Right mouse button  menus
  W A S D, mouse wheel, mouse at the screen edge   scroll
  M                   opens or closes the overview map
  0 1 2 3             pause, slow, medium, fast
  b r p t x z         tool shortcuts as in the original (bulldozer,
                      road, park, wire, rail, query)
  Esc                 closes the active window; quits when none is open
  Help                this guide

  In the overview map: click or drag to scroll the city.
@endnode

@node WINDOWS "Windows"
@toc MAIN

  Messages, Budget, Evaluation, Graphs, the Query box and the overview
  Map are normal Amiga windows on the game screen: drag them by the
  title bar and close them with the close gadget (the budget window's
  close gadget means Continue).

  The screen title bar can be dragged down to see the Workbench.
@endnode

@node MENUS "Menus"
@toc MAIN

  Project    new city, load, save, About, Help, quit
  Speed      pause / slow / medium / fast
  Options    auto bulldoze, auto budget, disasters, auto goto, city animation,
             world animation, messages, message windows, sound options (window with the
             switches and volume sliders), traffic rules, ask screen mode
  Level      Easy / Medium / Hard (start funds of a new city)
  Language   Automatic (system setting) / English / Deutsch / Polski (next start)
  Windows    budget, evaluation, graphs, map
  Map        overlays: power, traffic, pollution, crime, land value ...
  Disasters  fire, flood, tornado, earthquake, monster, meltdown
  Scenarios  historic cities with a story and a goal
@endnode

@node TRAFFIC "Traffic rules"
@toc MAIN

  Menu Options/Traffic rules (on by default in this version) switches these
  rules on and off:

  Jams        a busy road in front of a zone slows its growth.
  Rail        a zone whose trips go by rail grows better (up to +150, by the
              share of the way on rails); rail steps do not load the roads.
  Trips       a zone whose trips reach no destination grows less.
  Highway     tool at the bottom of the palette, 40 per tile, upkeep like five
              road tiles. A wide road without jams; it joins roads and other
              highways, goes on open land only and is no entrance for zones.
  Ports and   a sea port or airport with power and a road next to it links
  airports    separated areas: a trip that reaches a sea port goes on from
              another sea port on the same water, an airport links any
              airports (also over land). Ships and planes sail and fly there
              and back. A port or airport carries 1000 trips a year; when it is
              full the status line says so: build another one.

  The Query tool shows the traffic on roads, zones, ports and airports
  (traffic, rail link, effect on growth, linked ports, use this year/last year).

  Cities with highways cannot be loaded correctly by the original Micropolis.
@endnode

@node ANIMATION "Animation"
@toc MAIN

  Options/City animation switches the movement in the city itself (cars on
  the roads and highways, smoke, ...). Options/World animation switches the
  surf along the coasts (waves that roll in and run back) and the gusts of wind
  that pass over woods. Both are separate so that a slow machine can do without
  the second.
@endnode

@node DEMAND "The R C I bars"
@toc MAIN

  The three bars at the top right show the demand for Residential,
  Commercial and Industrial zones. Up means people want more of it,
  down means there is too much.
@endnode

@node SCENARIOS "Scenarios"
@toc MAIN

  Dullsville 1900, San Francisco 1906 (earthquake), Hamburg 1944 (fire
  bombing), Bern 1965 (traffic), Tokyo 1957 (monster), Detroit 1972
  (crime), Boston 2010 (nuclear meltdown), Rio de Janeiro 2047 (flood).
  Each has a time limit and a goal; the story is shown when it starts.
@endnode

@node SETTINGS "Screen mode and settings"
@toc MAIN

  At start a screen mode requester lists the usable RTG modes (640x480
  up to 800x600). You can choose "always use it"; Options/Ask for screen
  mode at start turns the question on again.

  Settings are stored in ENVARC:Micropolis.prefs. ToolTypes of the icon:
  SIZE=800x600 (fixed size, no question), CITY=<file>, LANGUAGE=deutsch (or
  english, polski; also lang=deutsch on the command line).
@endnode

@node CHEATS "Cheat words"
@toc MAIN

  As in the original, a few words typed in the game window have effects
  (for example "fund"). They are meant for fun; try them at your own risk.
@endnode

@node INDEX "Index"
@toc MAIN

  @{"Budget" link MENUS}   @{"Cheats" link CHEATS}   @{"Keys" link KEYS}
  @{"Scenarios" link SCENARIOS}   @{"Screen mode" link SETTINGS}
  @{"Tools" link TOOLS}   @{"Windows" link WINDOWS}
  @{"Traffic" link TRAFFIC}   @{"Animation" link ANIMATION}
@endnode
